    "body": "> It'd be ideal if one of these two locations contained the information, and the other linked to it, instead of duplicating it in both places.\n\nAgreed—see https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2014/commits/a4181637474e12e76c9aab4179931b99132ba9d2, which drops the first note entirely and also includes these changes:\n- Drop unnecessary RFC 2119 “must” for description of `rel=noopener` in the non-normative table summarizing link types (`rel` values)\n- Replace “_will not have an opener browsing context_” in two places with more-precise (and more-consistent with other parts of the spec) “_will have disowned its opener_” (the spec section where “_disowned its owner_” is `dfn`’ed is the central place in the spec we want people looking at for the relevant UA requirements/effects)\n",
